Subject: mod-amxb-rbus: weak fallback for rbusConfig_Get on rdkcentral rbus

The prpl-foundation fork of rbus exports rbusConfig_Get() for reading
runtime timeout config.  The rdkcentral fork (used by RDK-B) does not.

mod-amxb-rbus v1.3.2 was built against the prpl fork's headers; without
that symbol it fails to load at runtime with:

    /usr/bin/timingila: symbol lookup error:
      /usr/bin/mods/amxb/mod-amxb-rbus.so: undefined symbol: rbusConfig_Get

…and lcm-timingila.service exits 127 in a loop.

Fix: declare and define the symbol as __attribute__((weak)) so the .so
links cleanly.  At dynamic-load time, a strong rbusConfig_Get from a
future librbus that ships one will override the weak fallback; otherwise
the weak one is used and returns NULL.

amxb_rbus_set_timeout() already guards the result with when_null(...),
so a NULL return makes the timeout setter a no-op (rbus uses its
compiled-in defaults).  No behavioural change for AMX clients that
don't override the default rbus timeouts.

Upstream: rdkcentral/rbus would need to gain rbusConfig_Get for this
shim to be retired.  Until then this is the bridge.
---
 src/amxb_rbus_timeouts.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/amxb_rbus_timeouts.c b/src/amxb_rbus_timeouts.c
--- a/src/amxb_rbus_timeouts.c
+++ b/src/amxb_rbus_timeouts.c
@@ -73,7 +73,12 @@ typedef struct _rbusConfig_t {

 // LUCKELY THIS SYMBOL IS EXPORTED BY LIBRBUS, SO IT CAN BE CALLED
 // AND THE TIMEOUT CONFIG CAN BE RETRIEVED
-rbusConfig_t* rbusConfig_Get(void);
+// vCPE: rdkcentral rbus does NOT export this.  Provide a weak fallback
+// so the module loads; amxb_rbus_set_timeout() handles NULL gracefully.
+__attribute__((weak)) rbusConfig_t* rbusConfig_Get(void);
+__attribute__((weak)) rbusConfig_t* rbusConfig_Get(void) {
+    return NULL;
+}

